- op: discuss  # 8712
  at: '2026-10-27T21:26:30Z'  # 8712
  by: agent  # 8712
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8712
  clock: 4  # 8712
  nonce: '8712'  # 8712
  message: "2026-10-27 INVESTIGATION (owner-requested; ADR-0049/0050, INV-zumin, code, all 39 primitives). Recommendation: option (1), amend ADR-0050 section 1. The rows match what the mechanism was built for; the axiom sentence is narrower than the mechanism.\n\nFACTS\n- The simultaneous flag was minted (INV-zumin, IoPrimitive docstring) for a call that is TRUE under several boundaries at once; its worked example is a launch that also writes. WI-rutup's section 1 sentence later described one use of it, the content or chooser READING.\n- Consumers treat a simultaneous edge as reaching ALL its boundaries: boundaries_of(), compute_boundary_map's one-chain-per-boundary fan-out, taint minting per boundary. \"Primary\" is only the scalar meta.io_boundary, set first-declared-wins by CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES order. Its 5 readers are presence checks or fan-outs, and boundaries_of's docstring calls a scalar reader a bug.\n- So the stored \"primary\" is not the axiom's primary: for the 6 URL rows the scalar is env_read, while section 1 says the medium (navigation_read) is primary.\n- ADR-0049 ruling 1 / INV-lozat already justify the 23 ipc_recv+subprocess rows, each a launch plus a transfer of the child's bytes at the call.\n\nTHE 39 under the widened rule (\"a simultaneous boundary is a reading of the same crossing that a taint label needs, OR a second crossing the same call performs AT THIS CALL SITE that itself satisfies the axiom\"):\n- hold, 32: ipc_recv+subprocess 23; env_read+navigation_read 6; erlang filelib.ensure_dir (fs_read+fs_write); python builtins.license (fs_read+logging); objc NSURLConnection sendSynchronousRequest (net_send+net_recv).\n- fail, 4:\n  - scala Process.apply / Process.Process / Process.run (fs_write+subprocess). apply builds a ProcessBuilder and launches nothing; the fs_write is what the child may do later, which the axiom's \"not what the program is arranged to do later\" clause excludes. That is WI-novap.\n  - objc NSURLConnection sendAsynchronousRequest's net_recv: the response arrives in completionHandler, a deferred receive. That is WI-mapim's shape (it names NSURLSession; this row is the same).\n- judgment, 3: python platform.architecture / platform / processor (host_info_read+subprocess). The returned data's medium is the child's stdout (ipc_recv), its content host description. Keep: ipc_recv would mint untrusted_input for host facts, and host_info_read works here as the reading the host_description label needs.\n\nPROPOSED section 1 text (the third sentence): \"A `simultaneous` second boundary records either a reading of the same crossing that a taint label needs (as above), or a second crossing the same call performs at this call site, which must satisfy this axiom on its own. Every simultaneous boundary is a fact about the call, and consumers read them all (`boundaries_of`). The scalar `io_boundary` is the first declared in vocabulary order and carries no primacy.\""  # 8712
- op: discuss  # bc38
  at: '2026-10-27T21:41:05Z'  # bc38
  by: agent  # bc38
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bc38
  clock: 5  # bc38
  nonce: bc38  # bc38
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-10-27 (in session): yes to the amendment. ADR-0050 section 1 is widened: a simultaneous second boundary is either a reading of the same crossing that a taint label needs, or a second crossing the same call performs at this call site, which must satisfy the axiom on its own; every simultaneous boundary is a fact consumers read (boundaries_of), and the scalar io_boundary carries no primacy. Rows that fail it stay with WI-novap (scala Process.*) and WI-mapim (NSURLConnection async)."  # bc38
