  message: "Done in PR #1907 (ff3be24026), on the owner ruling above. ADR-0050 section 1 now says a simultaneous second boundary is a reading the taint label needs, or a second crossing the same call performs at this call site that satisfies the axiom on its own, and that none is primary. The ADR records the check of all 39 primitives: 32 hold, 3 are kept by judgment (python platform.*), 4 fail and are already filed (WI-novap, WI-mapim). The same sentence was updated in io_boundary_types, the concept-axes generator and docs/concept-axes.md, and the falsifiability survey. Docs only; no rows changed, so there is no behaviour to re-run."  # c4cb
